{"page":726,"blocks":[{"x":0.04849,"y":0.05257,"w":0.36456,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"712 Chapter 12: Vectors and the Geometry of Space"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.09343,"w":0.59305,"h":0.05885,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"addition), where the sum, called the resultant vector, is the diagonal of the parallelogram. In physics, forces add vectorially as do velocities, accelerations, and so on. So the force acting on a particle subject to two gravitational forces, for example, is obtained by adding the two force vectors."},{"x":0.09022,"y":0.11922,"w":0.02429,"h":0.01025,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"1.5u"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.15481,"w":0.5931,"h":0.04351,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"Figure 12.13 displays a geometric interpretation of the product ku of the scalar k and vector u. If k 7 0, then ku has the same direction as u; if k 6 0, then the direction of ku is opposite to that of u. Comparing the lengths of u and ku, we see that"},{"x":0.14715,"y":0.17149,"w":0.09141,"h":0.01094,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"2u −2u"},{"x":0.41668,"y":0.19546,"w":0.40467,"h":0.02741,"fs":0.01401,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"0 ku0 = 2(ku1)2 + (ku2)2 + (ku3)2 = 2k2(u1 2 + u2 2 + u3 2)"},{"x":0.04882,"y":0.20248,"w":0.23883,"h":0.01228,"fs":0.01151,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"FIGURE 12.13 Scalar multiples of u."},{"x":0.52892,"y":0.21848,"w":0.16228,"h":0.02741,"fs":0.01353,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"2 + u2 2 + u3 2 = 0 k0 0 u0 ."},{"x":0.44965,"y":0.23015,"w":0.07833,"h":0.01573,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"= 2k22u1"},{"x":0.32333,"y":0.25457,"w":0.59307,"h":0.02816,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"The length of ku is the absolute value of the scalar k times the length of u. The vector (-1)u = -u has the same length as u but points in the opposite direction."},{"x":0.10656,"y":0.27396,"w":0.03127,"h":0.01076,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"u −v"},{"x":0.35276,"y":0.2846,"w":0.33216,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The difference u - v of two vectors is defined by"},{"x":0.55086,"y":0.30762,"w":0.13388,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"u - v = u + (-v)."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.32088,"w":0.30427,"h":0.02475,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"If u = 8u1, u2, u39 and v = 8v1, v2, v39, then"},{"x":0.48863,"y":0.3439,"w":0.25832,"h":0.0251,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"u - v = 8u1 - v1, u2 - v2, u3 - v39."},{"x":0.11282,"y":0.35956,"w":0.01453,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"(a)"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.37668,"w":0.59304,"h":0.02882,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Note that (u - v) + v = u, so adding the vector (u - v) to v gives u (Figure 12.14a). Figure 12.14b shows the difference u - v as the sum u + (-v)."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.42064,"w":0.54383,"h":0.02323,"fs":0.01407,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 3 Let u = 8-1, 3, 19 and v = 84, 7, 09. Find the components of"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.45261,"w":0.26872,"h":0.02323,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"(a) 2u + 3v (b) u - v (c) ` 1"},{"x":0.58386,"y":0.45261,"w":0.03302,"h":0.03044,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"2 u ` ."},{"x":0.21508,"y":0.47326,"w":0.01745,"h":0.01076,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"−v"},{"x":0.07608,"y":0.49649,"w":0.05088,"h":0.01076,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"u + (−v)"},{"x":0.32333,"y":0.49673,"w":0.05909,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Solution"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.51016,"w":0.58574,"h":0.04241,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"(a) 2u + 3v = 28-1, 3, 19 + 384, 7, 09 = 8-2, 6, 29 + 812, 21, 09 = 810, 27, 29 (b) u - v = 8-1, 3, 19 - 84, 7, 09 = 8-1 - 4, 3 - 7, 1 - 09 = 8-5, -4, 19"},{"x":0.11773,"y":0.52071,"w":0.01526,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"(b)"},{"x":0.04881,"y":0.54415,"w":0.19912,"h":0.04297,"fs":0.01151,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"FIGURE 12.14 (a) The vector u - v, when added to v, gives u. (b) u - v = u + (-v)."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.56388,"w":0.04591,"h":0.02323,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"(c) ` 1"},{"x":0.36105,"y":0.56388,"w":0.23111,"h":0.0317,"fs":0.01329,"n":5,"k":0,"t":"2u ` = ` h- 1 2, 3 2, 1 2 i ` = Ca- 1 2b"},{"x":0.5938,"y":0.56388,"w":0.04868,"h":0.02255,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"2 + a3"},{"x":0.63431,"y":0.56388,"w":0.01711,"h":0.03044,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"2b"},{"x":0.65307,"y":0.56388,"w":0.04868,"h":0.02255,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"2 + a1"},{"x":0.69357,"y":0.56388,"w":0.01711,"h":0.03044,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"2b"},{"x":0.71233,"y":0.56394,"w":0.03817,"h":0.02316,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"2 = 1"},{"x":0.74232,"y":0.57432,"w":0.0479,"h":0.01999,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"2 211."},{"x":0.35277,"y":0.61268,"w":0.45259,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Vector operations have many of the properties of ordinary arithmetic."},{"x":0.35359,"y":0.65297,"w":0.27053,"h":0.02816,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Properties of Vector Operations Let u, v, w be vectors and a, b be scalars."},{"x":0.35359,"y":0.69068,"w":0.4758,"h":0.09021,"fs":0.01279,"n":9,"k":0,"t":"1. u + v = v + u 2. (u + v) + w = u + (v + w) 3. u + 0 = u 4. u + (-u) = 0 5. 0u = 0 6. 1u = u 7. a(bu) = (ab)u 8. a(u + v) = au + av 9. (a + b)u = au + bu"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.80797,"w":0.58891,"h":0.02814,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"These properties are readily verified using the definitions of vector addition and multi- plication by a scalar. For instance, to establish Property 1, we have"},{"x":0.49108,"y":0.8359,"w":0.24058,"h":0.02475,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"u + v = 8u1, u2, u39 + 8v1, v2, v39"},{"x":0.54007,"y":0.85508,"w":0.2036,"h":0.08078,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"= 8u1 + v1, u2 + v2, u3 + v39 = 8v1 + u1, v2 + u2, v3 + u39 = 8v1, v2, v39 + 8u1, u2, u39 = v + u."}]}